538
00:29:17.020 --> 00:29:18.428
Operation, and Safe?

539
00:29:18.708 --> 00:29:21.033
(PostgreSQL), and Safe approach.

540
00:29:21.313 --> 00:29:22.593
Add nullable column.

541
00:29:22.873 --> 00:29:23.599
Safe?

542
00:29:23.879 --> 00:29:25.201
(PostgreSQL):

543
00:29:25.481 --> 00:29:27.060
Fast (metadata only).

544
00:29:27.340 --> 00:29:29.196
Add column with constant default.

545
00:29:29.476 --> 00:29:30.201
Safe?

546
00:29:30.481 --> 00:29:31.804
(PostgreSQL):

547
00:29:32.084 --> 00:29:33.727
Fast since PG 11.

548
00:29:34.007 --> 00:29:36.097
Add NOT NULL to an existing column.

549
00:29:36.377 --> 00:29:37.103
Safe?

550
00:29:37.383 --> 00:29:38.705
(PostgreSQL):

551
00:29:38.985 --> 00:29:41.055
Scans the table under a strong lock.

552
00:29:41.335 --> 00:29:42.380
Safe approach:

553
00:29:42.660 --> 00:29:47.823
Add CHECK (col IS NOT NULL) NOT VALID, then VALIDATE CONSTRAINT, then SET NOT NULL.

554
00:29:48.103 --> 00:29:49.233
Create index.

555
00:29:49.513 --> 00:29:50.239
Safe?

556
00:29:50.519 --> 00:29:51.841
(PostgreSQL):

557
00:29:52.121 --> 00:29:53.188
Blocks writes.

558
00:29:53.468 --> 00:29:54.513
Safe approach:

559
00:29:54.793 --> 00:30:01.151
CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY (outside a transaction; retry if it fails, drop the INVALID leftovers).

560
00:30:01.431 --> 00:30:02.519
Add foreign key.

561
00:30:02.799 --> 00:30:03.524
Safe?

562
00:30:03.804 --> 00:30:05.127
(PostgreSQL):

563
00:30:05.407 --> 00:30:06.815
Validates under lock.

564
00:30:07.095 --> 00:30:08.140
Safe approach:

565
00:30:08.420 --> 00:30:11.108
NOT VALID, then VALIDATE CONSTRAINT separately.

566
00:30:12.458 --> 00:30:15.125
Rename or drop a column used by running code.

567
00:30:15.405 --> 00:30:16.130
Safe?

568
00:30:16.410 --> 00:30:17.733
(PostgreSQL):

569
00:30:18.013 --> 00:30:19.207
Breaks old pods.

570
00:30:19.487 --> 00:30:20.533
Safe approach:

571
00:30:20.813 --> 00:30:25.463
Expand, then migrate, then contract across releases (Ch 28).

572
00:30:25.743 --> 00:30:27.045
Change column type.

573
00:30:27.325 --> 00:30:28.050
Safe?

574
00:30:28.330 --> 00:30:29.653
(PostgreSQL):

575
00:30:29.933 --> 00:30:31.426
Often rewrites the table.

576
00:30:31.706 --> 00:30:32.751
Safe approach:

577
00:30:33.031 --> 00:30:35.122
New column + backfill + switch.

578
00:30:36.472 --> 00:30:46.819
Always set locktimeout for migrations (for example 5 s), so a migration waiting behind a long transaction doesn't queue every subsequent query behind itself.

579
00:30:48.169 --> 00:30:50.622
