00:38:52.415 --> 00:38:53.780
Here is a quick table:

727
00:38:54.060 --> 00:38:56.620
Option, and Pros, and Cons, and Verdict.

728
00:38:56.900 --> 00:38:59.673
JPA read-modify-write (status quo).

729
00:38:59.953 --> 00:39:00.807
Pros:

730
00:39:01.087 --> 00:39:01.919
Familiar.

731
00:39:02.199 --> 00:39:03.009
Cons:

732
00:39:03.289 --> 00:39:05.081
Lost updates at READ COMMITTED.

733
00:39:05.361 --> 00:39:06.172
Verdict:

734
00:39:06.452 --> 00:39:09.844
Rejected (incident). @Version optimistic locking.

735
00:39:10.124 --> 00:39:10.977
Pros:

736
00:39:11.257 --> 00:39:12.516
Detects conflicts.

737
00:39:12.796 --> 00:39:13.607
Cons:

738
00:39:13.887 --> 00:39:18.217
Hot rows cause retry storms (50 conflicts per second on one row).

739
00:39:18.497 --> 00:39:19.308
Verdict:

740
00:39:19.588 --> 00:39:22.489
Rejected for counters; kept for admin edits.

741
00:39:22.769 --> 00:39:23.601
SELECT...

742
00:39:23.881 --> 00:39:25.439
FOR UPDATE then compute.

743
00:39:25.719 --> 00:39:26.572
Pros:

744
00:39:26.852 --> 00:39:27.833
Explicit.

745
00:39:28.113 --> 00:39:28.924
Cons:

746
00:39:29.204 --> 00:39:31.359
Longer lock hold, more round trips.

747
00:39:31.639 --> 00:39:32.449
Verdict:

748
00:39:32.729 --> 00:39:35.481
Used only where logic can't be a single UPDATE.

749
00:39:35.761 --> 00:39:37.553
SERIALIZABLE for everything.

750
00:39:37.833 --> 00:39:38.687
Pros:

751
00:39:38.967 --> 00:39:39.884
Strongest.

752
00:39:40.164 --> 00:39:40.975
Cons:

753
00:39:41.255 --> 00:39:44.711
Aborts under contention; retry complexity everywhere.

754
00:39:44.991 --> 00:39:45.801
Verdict:

755
00:39:46.081 --> 00:39:49.217
Reserved for ledger invariants (Ch 45).

756
00:39:50.567 --> 00:39:54.365
Atomic conditional UPDATE, sorted lock order, CHECK constraints.

757
00:39:54.645 --> 00:39:55.498
Pros:

758
00:39:55.778 --> 00:40:00.279
One round trip per line, minimal lock time, DB-enforced invariant.

759
00:40:00.559 --> 00:40:01.370
Cons:

760
00:40:01.650 --> 00:40:03.165
Hot-row ceiling remains.

761
00:40:03.445 --> 00:40:04.255
Verdict:

762
00:40:04.535 --> 00:40:05.367
Chosen.

763
00:40:05.647 --> 00:40:07.205
Redis counters (DECRBY).

764
00:40:07.485 --> 00:40:08.338
Pros:

765
00:40:08.618 --> 00:40:09.642
Very fast.

766
00:40:09.922 --> 00:40:10.733
Cons:

767
00:40:11.013 --> 00:40:15.450
Not in the same transaction as the reservation and outbox; durability.

768
00:40:15.730 --> 00:40:16.541
Verdict:

769
00:40:16.821 --> 00:40:21.621
Rejected for the source of truth (Ch 46 discusses a Redis front-gate).

770
00:40:22.971 --> 00:40:23.653
8.

771
00:40:23.933 --> 00:40:25.085
Failure modes.

772
00:40:25.365 --> 00:40:31.424
A deadlock (shouldn't happen, given ordering) or a serialization failure: bounded retry with jitter.

