1195
01:04:07.987 --> 01:04:13.726
Keep dead tuples low. statementtimeout, locktimeout, idleintransactionsessiontimeout.

1196
01:04:14.006 --> 01:04:15.414
Typical starting point:

1197
01:04:15.694 --> 01:04:18.638
2 s or 1 s or 10 s for OLTP roles.

1198
01:04:18.918 --> 01:04:19.814
Guidance:

1199
01:04:20.094 --> 01:04:21.374
Server-side guards.

1200
01:04:21.654 --> 01:04:25.686
Hibernate jdbc.batchsize, orderinserts, orderupdates.

1201
01:04:25.966 --> 01:04:27.374
Typical starting point:

1202
01:04:27.654 --> 01:04:28.955
50, true, true.

1203
01:04:29.235 --> 01:04:30.131
Guidance:

1204
01:04:30.411 --> 01:04:31.777
With SEQUENCE ids.

1205
01:04:33.127 --> 01:04:34.599
defaultbatchfetchsize.

1206
01:04:34.879 --> 01:04:36.287
Typical starting point:

1207
01:04:36.567 --> 01:04:38.081
16 to 64.

1208
01:04:38.361 --> 01:04:39.257
Guidance:

1209
01:04:39.537 --> 01:04:42.204
Blunt but effective N+1 mitigation.

1210
01:04:43.554 --> 01:04:44.279
Cost.

1211
01:04:44.559 --> 01:04:46.031
RAM is the lever.

1212
01:04:46.311 --> 01:04:50.386
A working set that fits in memory turns disk reads into cache hits.

1213
01:04:50.666 --> 01:04:54.015
Size instances by working set, not by total data.

1214
01:04:54.295 --> 01:04:57.666
Indexes cost storage, RAM and write I or O.

1215
01:04:57.946 --> 01:04:59.205
Drop unused ones.

1216
01:04:59.485 --> 01:05:06.759
Read replicas are cheaper than a bigger primary for read-heavy loads, and each adds a cross-AZ replication traffic cost.

1217
01:05:07.039 --> 01:05:12.821
Partitioning plus archiving moves cold data to object storage at a fraction of the price.

1218
01:05:14.171 --> 01:05:23.600
Managed services (RDS or Aurora, Cloud SQL, Azure) trade higher unit cost for less operational toil (patching, backups, failover).

1219
01:05:23.880 --> 01:05:25.949
For most teams, that's the right trade.

1220
01:05:26.229 --> 01:05:35.872
The expensive database is usually a query problem: one missing index or an N+1 can cost more CPU than the rest of the workload combined.

1221
01:05:36.152 --> 01:05:39.352
Review pgstatstatements before scaling hardware.

